good evening we start the news hour with  some breaking news and president Trump  has imposed tough new sanctions on Iran  specifically targeted at the country's  supreme leader in response to the  shooting down of an American drone mr.  Trump says the United States does not  want conflict but Iran will not be  allowed to get nuclear weapons  our correspondent Amanda Walker joins me  from Washington so Amanda he pulled back  at the last moment from military action  but new sanctions announced now new  sanctions they flirted with military  action didn't they and they seem now  confident that economic punishment is  the way forward with Iran so this is  just coming in to us mark as we speak he  has confirmed that he's signing an  executive order imposing hard-hitting  sanctions on Iran going straight to the  top saying that the order will deny the  supreme leader and others access to  financial instruments Donald Trump says  we will continue to increase pressure on  Tehran never can Iran have a nuclear  weapon which ultimately is what these  sanctions are all about now in the  run-up to getting ready for that  military strike apparently Donald Trump  was told by his Secretary of State that  the maximum pressure campaign which is  really these sanctions is having the  desired effect some analysts say that  Iran's oil revenue is down 2/3 so I  think he certainly feels bolstered by  that and that's why they're continuing  with this he says that the new executive  order on sanctions was going to happen  regardless of the drones shoot down and  of course the deal maker in chief also  adding that he would love to get a deal  with Iran he says I think a lot of  restraint has been shown by us but that  doesn't mean we're going to show it in  the future and that echoes what he said  in an interview over the weekend he said  we don't want to go to war but if we did  it would be obliteration it's a  possibility he likes to use that as a  threat really while saying economic  sanctions are the way we  is basically the best way to get around  to start complying to start showing that  it's going to back down that so far  maximum pressure is only being met with  maximum defiance and resistance as we  can see those continued acts that the  Trump administration say is pure  provocation whether it's the oil tankers  the shooting down of the drone so far  it's hard to see how this campaign is  working other than the fact that the  economy in Iran is really struggling  yeah okay a man who just stay there a  second I think we can hear now from  President Trump about these sanctions  signing an executive order imposing  hard-hitting sanctions on the supreme  leader of Iran and the office of the  Supreme Leader of Iran and many others  today's action follows a series of  aggressive behaviors by the Iranian  regime in recent weeks including  shooting down of US drones and you shut  down the drone that's I guess everyone  saw that one and many other things  they've done many other things aside  from the individual drone you saw the  tankers and we know of other things that  were done also which were not good and  not appropriate the Supreme Leader of  Iran is one who ultimately is  responsible for the hostile conduct of  the regime he's respected within his  country his office oversees the regime's  most brutal instruments and clearly the  Islamic Revolutionary Guard for  sanctions imposed through the executive  order that I'm about to sign will deny  the Supreme Leader and the Supreme  Leader's office and those closely  affiliated with him and the office  access to key financial resources and  support the assets of Ayatollah Khomeini  and his office will not be spared from  the sanctions these measures represent a  strong and proportionate response to  Iran's increasingly provocative actions  we will continue to increase pressure on  terrorists until the regime abandons its  dangerous activities and its aspirations  including the pursuit of nuclear weapons  increased enrichment of uranium  development of ballistic missiles and  changement and support for terrorism  fuelling of foreign conflicts and  belligerent acts directed against the  United States and its allies the  agreement that was signed was a disaster  it was not doing what it was supposed to  do many bad things were taking place and  most importantly it was so short-term  that within a very short number of years  they would be able to make nuclear  weapons and that's unacceptable  never can Iran have a nuclear weapon  also included in this is we want the  stoppage immediately of their sponsoring  of terrorism they sponsor terrorism of  the level that nobody's ever seen before  and that's been over the last number of  years and they've taken all of that  money that was given to them by the past  administration and much of it was given  out to terrorist organizations in fact I  remember when John Kerry was asked a  question about whether or not this money  will be spent for terror he actually  said yes or at least he was referring to  some of it but he said yes it will be it  will be used for terror with if you can  believe that we give it a money we're  saying yes he can be used to terror that  was not a good answer  but that was the least of it frankly so  America is a peace-loving nation we do  not seek conflict with Iran or any other  country I look forward to the day when  sanctions can be finally lifted and Iran  can become a peaceful prosperous and  productive nation that can go very  quickly it can be tomorrow it could also  be in years from now so I look forward  to discussing whatever I have to discuss  with anybody that wants to speak in the  meantime who knows what's going to  happen I can only tell you we cannot  ever let Iran have a nuclear weapon and  it won't happen and secondly and very  importantly we don't want money going  out to sponsor terror  so you're the number one sponsor of  Terror anywhere in the world so I'll  sign this order right now  and I want to thank our military I want  to thank all of the people that have  been working with me over the last  number of months on this I think a lot  of restraint has been shown by us a lot  of restraint and that doesn't mean we're  going to show it in the future but I  felt that we want to give give this a  chance give it a good chance because I  think Iran potentially has a phenomenal  future just and I say that about North  Korea too I've said it about North Korea  I think North Korea has a phenomenal  future and I think Iran also has a  phenomenal future and it would like to I  think a lot of people would like to see  them get to work on that great future so  I'll sign this now and I appreciate you  all being here thank you from signing  that order for tough new sanctions on  Iran Amanda Walker is still with us in  Washington Amanda interesting to see how  Europe reacts to this and also  interesting that he says there he still  wants talks and he he doesn't want  conflict is it significant that he's  targeting personally the supreme leader  Ayatollah how many has had his calls for  talks rejected by the leader so is this  a response to that but it's interesting  the sort of language that Trump is using  they're suggesting that Iran could have  a great future he's trying a bit of his  flattery that he has done with North  Korea suggesting that he could be the  person to take things into a completely  new era when it comes to US relations  and that really appeals to Donald Trump  the idea that he could have a  breakthrough on these issues that have  plagued the US for decades whether it's  North Korea Iran that he could be the  one to see a new dawn in those relations  he talked about showing restraint which  certainly some people here analysts have  been saying you know we criticize Donald  Trump a lot but in pulling back at the  11th hour he did show restraint  the next day the US and the world was in  a much better position than it would  have b